[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/driftingly/rector-laravel/issues/comments/5907513325","html_url":"https://github.com/driftingly/rector-laravel/issues/574#issuecomment-5907513325","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/driftingly/rector-laravel/issues/574","id":5907513325,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFNE1eM8AAAABYB1_7Q","user":{"login":"cyppe","id":591720,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MTcyMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/591720?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyppe","html_url":"https://github.com/cyppe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyppe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyppe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyppe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyppe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyppe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyppe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyppe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyppe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cyppe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-30T08:41:41Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T08:41:41Z","body":"Some context that may help decide the fix (checked 2026-09-30):\n\n- **Both symplify packages are flagged abandoned on Packagist**, without a replacement: `symplify/rule-doc-generator-contracts` (last release 11.2.0, 2024-03) and `symplify/rule-doc-generator` (12.2.5, 2024-08). Since Composer 2.7, `composer audit` fails on abandoned packages by default, so every project that requires `driftingly/rector-laravel` now fails the audit.\n- **The contracts are a runtime requirement here, not just for docs.** `src/AbstractRector.php` implements `Symplify\\RuleDocGenerator\\Contract\\DocumentedRuleInterface`, and all 131 rules build a `RuleDefinition` in `getRuleDefinition()`. The generator (require-dev) only feeds `composer docs` → `docs/rector_rules_overview.md`.\n- **Rector 2 made `getRuleDefinition()` optional:** see [rector-src UPGRADING.md, \"AbstractRector get focused on code\"](https://github.com/rectorphp/rector-src/blob/main/UPGRADING.md). `rector/rector` still uses the contracts internally, but ships them scoped inside its package, so its users don't see the abandoned flag.\n\n**Possible ways out:**\n1. Drop `DocumentedRuleInterface` and `getRuleDefinition()` from the rules, and keep the rules overview another way, for example generated from the test fixtures.\n2. Keep the descriptions but move the few value objects (`RuleDefinition`, `CodeSample`, `ConfiguredCodeSample`) into the `RectorLaravel` namespace, and remove the dependency.\n\n**Interim workaround for users:** a targeted ignore, which keeps failing on any other abandoned package:\n```json\n\"config\": {\n    \"policy\": {\n        \"abandoned\": {\n            \"ignore\": {\n                \"symplify/rule-doc-generator-contracts\": \"Required by driftingly/rector-laravel; see https://github.com/driftingly/rector-laravel/issues/574\"\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/driftingly/rector-laravel/issues/comments/5907513325/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]